@startuml 04-app-lab-effect-cycle
skinparam backgroundColor white
title Rastok — one outbound Call, real or simulated
skinparam shadowing false

actor Caller
participant "Worker / Lab" as Entry
participant "Execution" as Core
participant "DriverPoller" as Poller
database "Journal" as Journal
participant "RuntimeDrivers" as Routing
participant "Selected Driver" as Driver
participant "External system" as World

Caller -> Entry: execute checked plan
Entry -> Core: accept explicit typed input
Core -> Core: prepare identity, routes and capacity
Core -> Journal: commit INGRESS and selected routes
Core -> Routing: prepare exact request (no I/O)
Routing -> Driver: prepare_request
Driver --> Routing: PreparedRequest
Routing --> Core: PreparedRequest
Core -> Journal: commit EGRESS Call opening
Core -> Poller: poll committed Calls and responses
Poller -> Routing: start committed CallOpen
Routing -> Driver: start with original request

alt physical Driver
  Driver -> World: perform operation
  World --> Driver: physical response
else Lab substitute
  Driver -> Driver: evaluate scripted response or remain silent
end

Poller -> Routing: poll_responses
Routing -> Driver: poll_responses
Driver --> Routing: CallResponse
Routing -> Routing: check the owning Driver
Routing --> Poller: correlated CallResponse
Poller -> Poller: check completion against resolved Contract
Poller -> Journal: close EGRESS Call once
Poller --> Core: ClosedCall
Core -> Core: prepare Connector transaction and dispositions
Core -> Core: reserve delivery capacity
Core -> Journal: commit TRANSACTION with ordered emissions
Core -> Core: publish committed deliveries; apply Retry state
Core --> Entry: recorded state and causal evidence
Entry --> Caller: result and read-only projection

note over Core,Journal
The Call closure and Connector transaction are distinct records.
A closed Call waits if the transaction cannot reserve capacity.
A timeout is an execution decision, not a Driver response.
An outbound result is not a new INGRESS root.
Retry-held emissions are journaled, not delivered to the graph.
end note
note over Routing,World
Every exchange stays with its selected Driver object.
Drivers never assign envelope identities or write records.
Recovery does not repeat an already opened external operation.
end note
@enduml
